Story:
Five shots. Five shots rang out in the darkness of the night, echoing through my home and into my soul; 

 *Sixty-nine consecutive nights since I last had a drink. * 

 The silence was broken only by muffled sobbing that could be heard no more than miles away. It

I play the haunting melody of old-fangled folk songs, foul and dreary as they tumble from vile lips; 

 It is a foul thing to hear them sing in such a foul manner. 

 I sit upon my sickle, sickling forth fouls fouls fouls fouls
